# 🚀 OVERVIEW
# AutoYou2Face automatically fetches your latest YouTube video and posts 
# it directly to your Facebook Page every 30 minutes via GitHub Actions.
#
# =====================================================================
# 📋 STEP-BY-STEP GUIDE TO OBTAIN YOUR 4 SECRET KEYS
# =====================================================================
#
# 🔑 1. YOUTUBE_API_KEY
#    1. Go to Google Cloud Console: https://console.cloud.google.com
#    2. Log in with the Google account associated with your YouTube channel.
#    3. Click on the project selector at the top left and select "New Project".
#    4. Name your project (e.g., "AutoYou2Face-Project") and click "Create".
#    5. Navigate to "APIs & Services" > "Library".
#    6. Search for "YouTube Data API v3" and click "Enable".
#    7. Go to "APIs & Services" > "Credentials".
#    8. Click "+ Create Credentials" at the top and select "API key".
#    9. Copy the generated API key (format: AIzaSy...).
#
# 🔑 2. YOUTUBE_CHANNEL_ID
#    1. Log in to your YouTube account on a web browser.
#    2. Go directly to Advanced Settings: https://www.youtube.com/account_advanced
#    3. Locate the "Channel ID" field.
#    4. Copy the value (starts with "UC...", e.g., UCxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx).
#
# 🔑 3. META_ACCESS_TOKEN (Facebook Page Access Token)
#    1. Go to Meta Graph API Explorer: https://developers.facebook.com/tools/explorer
#    2. Log in with the Facebook account that administers your Page.
#    3. In the right panel, select your Meta App under "Meta App".
#    4. Under "User or Page", choose "Get Page Access Token" and select your target Facebook Page.
#    5. Under "Permissions", add the following 3 permissions:
#       - pages_read_engagement
#       - pages_show_list
#       - pages_manage_posts
#    6. Click the blue "Generate Access Token" button and accept the authorization prompts.
#    7. Copy the generated long string.
#    8. (Recommended) Convert this token into a Long-Lived Token using the Access Token Debugger tool
#       (https://developers.facebook.com/tools/debug/accesstoken) to prevent weekly expirations.
#
# 🔑 4. FB_PAGE_ID
#    1. Log in to Facebook and switch to your Facebook Page profile.
#    2. Go to the "About" section > "Page information" (or Settings > Page settings).
#    3. Locate the "Page ID" field.
#    4. Copy the numerical ID (e.g., 100123456789).
#
# =====================================================================
# ⚙️ METHOD A: CONFIGURE GITHUB ACTIONS VIA WEB INTERFACE
# =====================================================================
#
# 1. Open your repository on GitHub (https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/AutoYou2Face).
# 2. Click on the "Settings" tab in the top menu bar.
# 3. In the left sidebar, click on "Secrets and variables" > "Actions".
# 4. Click the green "New repository secret" button and add all 4 secrets:
#
#    Name: YOUTUBE_API_KEY      | Value: <your_youtube_api_key>
#    Name: YOUTUBE_CHANNEL_ID   | Value: <your_channel_id>
#    Name: META_ACCESS_TOKEN    | Value: <your_facebook_page_token>
#    Name: FB_PAGE_ID           | Value: <your_facebook_page_id>
#
# 5. Enable Write Permissions for GitHub Actions:
#    - In the left sidebar under "Settings", go to "Actions" > "General".
#    - Scroll down to "Workflow permissions".
#    - Select "Read and write permissions".
#    - Click "Save".
#
# 6. Test Your Setup:
#    - Go to the "Actions" tab at the top of your repository.
#    - Select "AutoYou2Face Publisher" from the left menu.
#    - Click "Run workflow" > "Run workflow" to trigger the initial test.
#    - The workflow will now execute automatically every 30 minutes!
#
# =====================================================================
# 💻 METHOD B: CONFIGURE GITHUB ACTIONS VIA CLI (gh)
# =====================================================================
#
# If you are using GitHub Codespaces or a local terminal with the GitHub CLI installed:
#
# 1. Authenticate with GitHub:
#    gh auth login
#
# 2. Navigate to your repository directory:
#    cd AutoYou2Face
#
# 3. Set all 4 secrets in one step:
#    gh secret set YOUTUBE_API_KEY --body "YOUR_YOUTUBE_API_KEY"
#    gh secret set YOUTUBE_CHANNEL_ID --body "YOUR_YOUTUBE_CHANNEL_ID"
#    gh secret set META_ACCESS_TOKEN --body "YOUR_META_ACCESS_TOKEN"
#    gh secret set FB_PAGE_ID --body "YOUR_FB_PAGE_ID"
#
# 4. Verify your configured secrets:
#    gh secret list
#
# 5. Trigger the first workflow run immediately:
#    gh workflow run auto_post.yml
#    gh run watch
#
